<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan CPC buys July fuel oil at around $124/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan CPC buys July fuel oil at around $124/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has bought one to two 38,000-tonne cargoes of 0.5-percent sulphur fuel oil at around $124 per tonne for July delivery, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>CPC bought the low-pour cargoes for delivery July 1-10 to Keelung, Taichung or Shenao on a cost-and-freight basis (c-and-f), the official said.</p>
<p>In its last fuel oil purchase, CPC bought two 38,000-tonne cargoes of 0.5-percent fuel oil at around $117 and $120 per tonne respectively for June 1-30 and June 11-30 deliveries.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65 8703571)</p>
</text>
